- LOST must not match LOST.
- FOUND must not match FOUND.
- A user's own report must not match their other report.
- Only OPEN reports should participate in new matching.
- A match should only be created after the similarity threshold is met.

Also ensure that matching both directions does not create two separate records for the same LOST/FOUND pair.

Expected result: Every eligible pair should have one persistent match record, regardless of which report was submitted first.

# 5. Change 3 – Correct Permanent Match Storage

Critical database reliability fix

File: `db/repository.ts`

This file handles the database operations for your Member 2 module.

