| Closed reports          | Rejected                                                |
| Reclaimed reports       | Rejected                                                |

## 13.2 Database and integration tests

Unit tests alone cannot establish that Atlas persistence works.

You also need integration tests.

| Test                            | Expected result                           |
| ------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------- |
| New LOST against existing FOUND | Match is created when eligible            |
| New FOUND against existing LOST | Match is created when eligible            |
| Below-threshold pair            | No match created                          |
| Duplicate pair                  | One match record only                     |
| Concurrent matching             | One permanent match record only           |
| Owner notification              | One notification created                  |
| Finder notification             | One notification created                  |
| Duplicate notification          | Prevented                                 |
| Unrelated user access           | Rejected                                  |
| Unauthorized verification       | Rejected                                  |
| Unauthorized recovery           | Rejected                                  |
| Recalculation                   | Returns actual saved match total          |
| Production seed endpoint        | Unavailable                               |
| Backend restart                 | Matches and notifications remain in Atlas |

